  "content": "The full article content could not be retrieved from the source page. The page returned a placeholder stating 'Just a moment...' and did not provide the body of the story; only the headline and metadata were available for extraction.\n\nAccording to the headline, Japanese author Keigo Higashino has died at the age of 68. No further details about the circumstances of his death were present on the retrieved page.\n\nHigashino was among Japan's best-known contemporary mystery writers, celebrated for tightly plotted crime novels and psychologically complex characters. He achieved international recognition, and several of his works reached audiences outside Japan through translations and screen adaptations. 'The Devotion of Suspect X' is often cited as one of his most widely read novels and helped introduce many readers to his style.\n\nThough the source content was unavailable, Higashino's influence on modern Japanese crime fiction is widely acknowledged. His novels often explored moral ambiguity, clever plotting, and human motivations, and adaptations of his work for film and television broadened his readership globally.\n\nAt the time this entry was prepared, no reliable details or confirmations from family, publishers, or official representatives were present on the retrieved page. Reporters and editors will seek additional sources and official statements to verify the report and provide further information.\n\nThis record will be updated as more information and reliable reporting become available. The inability to access the original article body was due to site protection on the source page.",
